diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 06eb2ea..6bdaa12 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -2,6 +2,10 @@
 
 ## Unreleased
 
+- Error responses carry a stable code: the body is now
+  `{"error": {"code": ..., "message": ...}, "status": ...}`. `HTTPError`
+  subclasses set `code`, defaulting to `http_<status>`. `ClientError.message`
+  reads the message from the new body.
 - `Client.options()` for sending preflight requests.
 
 ## 0.4.0
diff --git a/docs/reference.md b/docs/reference.md
index 4a4b9a0..bafa99c 100644
--- a/docs/reference.md
+++ b/docs/reference.md
@@ -31,7 +31,12 @@ pattern column is what the raw, still percent-encoded segment must match.
 | `MethodNotAllowed` | `405` | status; the response carries an `Allow` header |
 | `InternalError` | `500` | status of any unexpected exception when `debug` is off |
 | `HTTPError.message` | `status reason in lower case` | default message, e.g. `gone` for 410 |
-| `error_body` | `{"error": message, "status": status}` | JSON body of every error response |
+| `HTTPError.code` | `http_{status}` | default code of a subclass that sets none, e.g. `http_410` |
+| `error_body` | `{"error": {"code": code, "message": message}, "status": status}` | JSON body of every error response |
+| `code.BadRequest` | `bad_request` | error code |
+| `code.NotFound` | `not_found` | error code |
+| `code.MethodNotAllowed` | `method_not_allowed` | error code |
+| `code.InternalError` | `internal_error` | error code |
 | `Allow` | `sorted, comma-separated` | methods listed on a 405 |
 | `debug` | `False` | when true, unexpected exceptions propagate from `App.handle` |
 
